Vanilla NetHack 3.4.3

I finally got another ascension.  My first since March of 2005; my
fourth overall (one with 3.3.1 and three with 3.4.3)  I feel like I've
played a million times since the last time--I always have a character
going.  I've gotten close several times; but always seemed to get worn
down by the onslaught of monsters.

I got some wise words from posters here along the lines of "slow down
once you've met Rodney" and "take your time and think about each move".
 This time, I did just that.  I took my time.  I was very careful.  I
kept tabs of my inventory; uncursing items that became cursed and so
forth.  This was definitely a lot better way to play than the anxious
way I would play in the past.

As far as the game, here are a couple highlights:

[Following may be SPOILY]

1)  I've never done well with knights.  This time, however, I found a
wand of wishing at the very start.  I wished for +3b SDSM, +3bf CoMR,
and +3bf GoD and got them all at +3.  This enabled me to survive the
early game, which I was never able to do before with knights.

2) "oLS saved me from my own stupidity twice.  First I was saved after
bashing away at a fire elemental while not realizing that I was burning
to death.  The second was at the entrance to that big inside room with
monsters, on the way to Rodney, when a soldier hit me with a footrice
corpse.  Both times I was playing too fast.

3) No Fort Ludios (at least I never found the portal and I'm sure I
checked all levels below the Quest level for vaults)  I wasn't able to
buy protection all the way down to naked 1 or 2.  I did make use of
much of the $ in Gehennom to buy as much as I could from the priest of
Moloch in the Valley of the Dead.

4) As opposed to the "close but no cigar" games, Rodney did not conjure
monsters right away after he appeared and I was able to zap him with a
wand of death (got him 10 times).

5) Using the tactic of staying inside a vortex and healing up (with
resistance to the vortex of course) worked nicely in the Plane of Air.
I was able restore my health after each battle with the air elementals.

6) The first altar I went to on the Astral Plane was my lawful one!!
That saved a lot of fighting and greatly contributed to this win.

I believe that offensive power is something that I have not focused on
enough.  I probably lost the near ascension games because I didn't have
the offensive capability to fight through the hordes of monsters.  You
need to be able to take out weak monsters with one blow and to take out
the big guys with 2 or 3.  Otherwise, they will wear you down or cause
you to use up all of your inventory trying to get through them.

I had Excaliber at +6 or +5 and a +2 = of increase damage for most of
the game.  That combination did a great job of taking out monsters both
big and small.

Thanks and on to the next game!!
